ss lies at the center of the specimen and comes closest to within 0 4cm to the posterior  0 6cm from the anterior  1 5cm from the inferior and 2 2cm from the superior resection margins  The smaller mass comes closest to within 0 4cm to the closest posterior  0 7cm from the anterior  and 1 1cm from the superior resection margins  The smaller mass lies closest to within 0 5cm from the closest medial resection margin  The specimen is submitted as follows  C G  Large mass to resection margin  H I  Smaller mass to margin  J  Breast parenchyma away from the lesion  two representative sections  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast additional superior medial tissue  is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of tan yellow fibrofatty soft tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final shaved margins  medial half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan yellow lobular  focally hemorrhagic and cauterized soft tissue  The unoriented specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes L R  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margins  lateral half of cavity  right breast  are multiple tan yellow to focally hemorrhagic and cauterized fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x 3 8x 0 8cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes S V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 4cm tan yellow  lobulated  hemorrhagic and focally cauterized soft tissue with a long stitch marking an undesignated aspect  Also received in the same container  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue  Lymph nodes are separate from the undesignated ar