n by  KRISTEN SMITH Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY CAVITY COMING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE SUPERIOR MARGIN  NO RESIDUAL GROSSLY RECOGNIZED  O R  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Rosa Sung Eun Choi  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  1   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  AXILLARY   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  2  PART F  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  3    report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  19 AUG 98 at 13 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  AND PRESENT AT REMOVED_DATE CM  FROM THE RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not identified  No ductal carcinoma in situ is identified  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  21 AUG 98 at 17 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with an inserted localizing guide wire in place  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned at 0 3cm intervals to reveal a 0 4cm white  irregular area located 0 2cm from the inked margin  The lesion is too small to freeze and is entirely submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the specimen has unremarkable parenchyma and is entirely submitted in cassettes B through H  No frozen section is done  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS EXAMINATION ONLY BREAST  RIGHT   SINGLE SUSPICIOUS WHITE AREA MEASURING REMOVED_DATE CM AND LOCATED REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  JEROME T  O CONNELL JR   MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
