Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 12 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE TUBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  SEVERELY ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MINUTE FOCUS ASSOCIATED WITH INVASIVE COMPONENT  PRESENT  0 1 CM FROM AN INKED MARGIN  3  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal breast parenchyma with a firm area of fibrosis corresponding to the x ray findings  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A H  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  BENIGN  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
