  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  20 5   1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  20 10   1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  20 23  2  HLA DR     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  20 43   1  TdT     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     MPO    INTERPRETATION  1  Polyclonal  Kappa  and lambda    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   B cells  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   T cells  Note  There is no evidence for a monoclonal B or unusual T cell population   Analysis by Frederic I  Preffer  PhD  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 02 at 17 18     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS ON FROZEN AND PARAFFIN SECTIONS  HP  REMOVED_CASE_ID    With antibodies to immunoglobulin heavy and light chains there is polytypic staining of rare lymphoid cells  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of few small cells in a patchy and diffuse pattern  With antibody to T lineage associated antigens  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most small cells scattered within the tissue  With antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   leukocyte common antigen  most cells are stained  With antibody to cytokeratin there is staining of residual ducts  The necrotic cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and many nuclei stain for Ki 67  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of a largely reactive lymphoid infiltrate  The staining of cells in the necrotic area for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  could support the interpretation that this represents necrotic B cell lymphoma  However  nonspecific staining for these antigens can occur in foci of necrotic tissue  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 02 at 14 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only are small pieces of yellow tan rubbery fibrotic tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  Representative sections are submitted for frozen section diagnosis  Frozen section saved  the remaining tissue was submitted separately in B   formalin fixation and flow cytometry  The tissue fixed in B  is submitted in cassette A  The formalin fixed part of tissue is submitted in cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast   in disagreement with requisition which states left breast  are three pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette C  Resident  ANDRAS SCHAFFER  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH FIBROSIS AND PATCHY LYMPHOCYTIC INFILTRATES  LYMPHOMA WORK UP DONE  FROZEN SAVED  O R  Resident  MIN LI  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS LEFT  PART B  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPS