n and greater than 2 0cm from the inferior margin  The cavity surrounds firm  mottled tan yellow to tan white tissue  No other masses or nodules are grossly identified  The remainder of the tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections including the biopsy cavity  submitted from inferior to superior Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 10 47 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  TWO HIGHLY ATYPICAL GLANDS SUGGESTIVE OF RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID TYPE   MULTIFOCAL  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF EXTENSIVE  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  ONE OF 15 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  MICROMETASTATIS   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  FIBROSIS  RADIAL SCARS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  AND MULTIPLE SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  5  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  Note  Two severely atypical glands with features suggestive of residual invasive carcinoma are identified within the wall of the biopsy cavity  Microscopic foci of metastatic ductal carcinoma are identified within the subcapsular sinus of one lymph node  The foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are identified in five random sections taken distant from the biopsy site  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 08 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  Right breast   is a 24 x 17 x 4cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying 25 x 12cm tan skin ellipse which bears a 6cm  well healed scar  2 5cm medial to the 4cm in diameter  grossly unremarkable nipple  and a 2 5cm scar located 5cm lateral to the nipple  A 8 x 6 x 4cm axillary tail is identified  Cross sectioning reveals a 2cm in diameter  blood filled  well circumscribed biopsy cavity  3 5cm beneath the small scar in the lateral quadrant  3cm from the deep margin and 5cm from the lateral margins  The biopsy cavity is focally surrounded by white fibrous strands of tissue maximally 1cm in thickness  The remainder of the cavity is surrounded by yellow gray fat  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is rubbery  white tan  and intermixed with yellow strands of adipose tissue  No tumor is grossly identified  SECTION CODE  A  1 lymph node  bisected B I  representative sections of the other lymph nodes J Q  entire biopsy cavity R  old biopsy cavity from medial incision S CC  representative section of breast parenchyma DD  section through nipple  Resident  Sigrid Regauer  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Checked.
