ue of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a single mass containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail attached to a breast of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin flap and inverted nipple with a 3 0cm scar on the skin flap on the opposite side from the axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm gray area beneath the incisional scar containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hollow cavity and several 0 1cm nodules in the adjacent fat  Representative sections of the cavity are submitted in A through D  with E containing the closest margin  The specimen also contains other gray areas  representative sections are submitted in F through H  Lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes I through L  from distal to proximal  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue flap  are multiple fragments of adipose tissue and strips of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  representative sections are submitted in M and N  Gross Description by  ANTHONY FORRESTER  HMS Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  G  Gregory Gallico I