Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 02 CLINICAL DATA  Biopsy at outside hospital showed   ductal breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND HEMOSIDERIN DEPOSITION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 49                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  stitch on inferior margin    is a 11 x 7 x 6cm piece of breast tissue with a 8 x 2cm skin ellipse on its surface  A 3 7cm fine suture line courses longitudinally across the skin ellipse  The medial margin has been inked black  the lateral margin red  and the deep margin green  Sectioning through the breast tissue demonstrates a central area consisting of red brown hemorrhage surrounding tan white fibrous tissue that has a stellate appearance and intervening yellow  chalky  fatty appearing tissue  The fat away from the central area has a normal yellow  glistening appearance  Grossly  there are no areas suggestive of residual carcinoma  This central area  at its closest point from the resection margin  measures 0 4cm  The central area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm in total greatest dimensions  SLIDE INDEX  A   inferior margin B C   deep margin D   superior margin E   lateral margin F through M   sections through the biopsy cavity and adjacent breast tissue  Labeled  Right axillary content  is a 9 x 6 x 2cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue and intermixed lymph nodes  The largest node measures 1 8cm in diameter and on cut section is infiltrated with fat  A representative section from each node is submitted in cassettes N through U  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  David John Mikulis  M D  PART A  PRIOR RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY SITE PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  A FEW FOCI  CALCIFICATION IN MICROCYSTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protien  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone recptor protien  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  accompanied with a radiograph   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  tan to white  slightly gritty area extending to the margin  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm  Entirely submitted in A through J  with the suspicious area in A through H  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Checked.
