ially sectioned perpendicular to the mediolateral axis into twelve slices numbered from lateral to medial  The internal portion of the specimen is primarily unremarkable adipose tissue  The remainder of the specimen  slices  4    12  primarily contain tan white  soft to rubbery tissue  which extensively abuts the superior edge of the specimen  as well as abutting the superior half of the anterior and posterior edges  The inferior aspect is primarily lined by adipose tissue  however  there are strands of white fibrous appearing tissue  which extend from main fibrous focus and reach the inferior margin  A biopsy tract is not clearly identified  however  the metal clip is identified in slice  6  at approximately the mid point of the specimen in all axes   Overall  the fibrous areas mass measure approximately 6 x 4 x 4cm  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  1  lateral margin   radially  entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  4  representative sections to superior and anterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  5  representative sections to superior  posterior  and inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  6  representative sections to include anterior and inferior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  6  center of fibrous area with clip site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  7  anterior and inferior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  8  inferior and anterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  9  anterior and superior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  10  inferior portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  12  medial margin   radially  entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of slide  6  entirely  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm aggregate of fibroadipose lymph node bearing tissue which is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REM