n is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast final margin deep   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of dense gray white fibrous tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a gray white homogeneous cut surface with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast final margin medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of dense gray white fibrous tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  T he stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a gray white homogeneous cut surface with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast final shaved lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of dense gray white fibrous tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a gray white  homogeneous cut surface with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paula Arnell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overex