acteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  06 AUG 02 at 17 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm specimen consisting of 2 lymph nodes  measuring in their diameter REMOVED_DATE  and 0 8cm  The nodes are bivalved and frozen as FX  1  and resubmitted as A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow portion of breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The anterior is inked black  the posterior is inked blue  and the superior rim is inked red  The specimen is serially sectioned revealing a tan white firm area with a focal hemorrhagic area consistent with biopsy cavity  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The firm area appears to grossly abut the anterior black and the posterior blue margins  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code  B C  Sections of the firm area with possible biopsy cavity which is in the medial portion of the specimen  D E  Other firm areas near the biopsy cavity in the middle portion of the specimen  F  Another firm area in the more lateral part of the specimen  G  A grossly uninvolved portion in the lateral part of the specimen  H  A grossly uninvolved area from the medial portion of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of yellow white breast tissue with a stitch designating the point furthest from the tumor  Half of the specimen on the stitch side is inked black and the side opposite the stitch is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned revealing tan white to yellow grossly unremarkable breast tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes I J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary lymph nodes contents  are 2 portions of yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  containing multiple lymph nodes REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  Section Code  K L  Sections of whole lymph nodes  M N  Each is 1 lymph node bisected and entirely submitted  O  The remaining fibroadipose tissue  Resident  VINCENT KO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  RIGHT   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  ONE OF TWO  O R  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE RIGHT  PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  LUMPECTOMY PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN PART D  LYMPH NODE CONTENTS  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION , Checked.
