nicates with the medial and posterior margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior margin is inked blue  the superior margin is inked green  and the inferior margin is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral to reveal diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue which hemorrhage and chalky yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  No discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  The specimen is entirely submitted  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the medial end margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the lateral end margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin  lateral half of cavity   are two irregular portions of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Sectioning reveals dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  final margin  medial half of cavity   are four irregular portions of gray white to tan pink fibrofatty tissue which aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Sectioning reveals dense gray white fibrous tissue  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Left   Reexcision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin  Lateral Half of Cavity   Excision PART C  Breast  Left  Final Margin  Medial Half of Cavity   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 22 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  Note  The resection margins are free of tumor  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MODERATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM INVASIVE TUMOR  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 5 OF 13 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  Note  Two positive lymph nodes  1 0CM in largest size  show complete replacement by tumor and a reactive histiocytic proliferation  necrosis and fibrosis  The remaining three positive lymph nodes each contain less than 0 2cm of tumor  Invasive adenocarcinoma is present in axillary tissue adjacent to lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a 21 x 15 x 4cm right modified radical mastectomy  Specimen with a 20 x 10cm overlying skin ellipse with a centrally located nipple and a 6 x 5 x 2 5cm axillary tail  The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm white yellow  focally cystic  firm mass of regular borders that is 0 1cm from the skin surface and 0 5cm from the deepest margin and 0 2cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  In the same mass  there is an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm of firm area that is 0 5cm from the deep margin  Representative section from the mass including the firm area are included in cassette A C and P S  Additional representative section from the mass are submitted in cassette D through I  A section away from the mass in cassette J  Lymph node dissected from the axillary tail are submitted in cassettes K through O  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    AXILLARY CONTENTS , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Rajni V Mandal  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Devon Gimbel  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Locally advanced triple negative invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST AND AXILLARY TISSUE  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  SLIGHT FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  CELLULAR CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA CELLS ARE IDENTIFIED WITHIN THE BREAST PARENCHYMA  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN 4 OF 4 NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  All of the candidate lymph nodes that are dissected from the modified radical mastectomy specimen and from the separately submitted left axillary tissue specimen have the appearance of fibroinflammatory nodules containing histiocytes  plasma cells  necrotic cellular material and focal hemosiderin deposits  Very rare isolated viable appearing tumor cells are identified in these nodules  Although the number of residual tumor cells is very small  the appearance is consistent with lymph nodes that may have been largely or completely replaced by tumor before chemotherapy treatment  Because of scarring  the presence or absence of extranodal extension cannot be assessed  No residual tumor cells are identified within the breast parenchyma  which has been extensively sampled for microscopic examination  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  ADDITIONAL   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN 5 OF 5 NODES  SEE NOTE ABOVE  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  SLIGHT FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY WITHIN THE BREAST  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE INCLUDED LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   315   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node  315   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue  with one REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lymph node that is frozen entirely as FX 1 and is now submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right simple mastectomy   is a 27 x 18 x 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen  with a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral margins  The anterior surface contains a 23 x 10 5cm light brown skin ellipse with a 3 5cm in diameter areola and a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly tan yellow  lobulated cut surface interspersed with moderate fibrous tissue  No discrete mass or lesion is appreciated  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from central quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left modified radical mastectomy   is a 26 x 20 x 5 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 3cm axillary tail  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch indicating the superior aspect and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is surfaced by a 23 x 10 5cm tan pink skin ellipse with a 4 x 3cm dark brown areola with an inverted nipple  Located 3cm medial to the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm dark brown discoloration  consistent with a previous biopsy site that is 1 5cm to the closest skin margin  No other scars or other skin lesions are grossly appreciated  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm indurated mass that is 1 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 4 8cm to the closest anterior margin  The mass is located in the central to lower inner quadrant of the breast  and immediately anterior to the mass  there is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of fibrous tissue  The remaining mammary tissue is fibrofatty with moderate amounts of fibrous and diffusely nodular tissue  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals 3 candidate lymph nodes ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining small portion of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple to underlying breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire skin biopsy site to closest skin margin  radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of centrally located fibrous tissue to areola   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  