Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA INVOLVING 14 OF 19 LYMPH NODES AND INVADING SMALL AXILLARY VEINS  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma exhibits both ductal and lobular features  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 41                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast and axillary contents  is a 780 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimenn with an axillary tail of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm and a skin ellipse is REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  such that the nipple is located 10 0cm from the medial end and 3 5cm from the superior cut border of the skin ellipse  The entire specimen is inked in black and the posterior surface is also double inked in green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm irregularly shaped white firm mass with a gritty cut surface  and a 1 0cm diameter biopsy cavity located at the anterior border of the tumor mass  The main bulk of the tumor mass extends to 0 5cm of the posterior resection margin  Irregularly shaped white to pink fibrous tissue radiate away from tumor mass both medially and laterally approaching the posterior resection margin  The nipple is retracted into the skin  Dissection of the axillary tail yield 19 lymph nodes of varying sizes from 0 5cm up to 1 5cm in length  The large nodes are bisected and many of which reveal a white central core surrounded by pink parenchyma  The tumor has a gritty cut surface  Section Code  A  section of the tumor mass from the biopsy cavity  B  tumor at the nearest resection margin  posterior   C  section of tumor at its lateral end near the posterior margin  D  section of tumor near the medial wall of the biopsy cavity  E  section 1 0cm medial from D  F  section on the medial inferior margin  G J  nodes from the axillary tail  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LET   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  95    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO THE RESECTION MARGINS AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is 0 5cm in size  There is focal perineural invasion  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL 