Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA  An 84 year old female with biopsy proven infiltrating ductal carcinoma  underwent right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CAUTERIZED INFERIOR MARGIN  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FIFTEEN OF FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES  0 15   BIOPSY SITE AND FAT NECROSIS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MICROCYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  FIBROSIS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  AND MICROCALCIFICATION IN BENIGN GLANDS   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The nipple is free of tumor  There are rare foci suspicious for lymphatic invasion  Focally  ductal carcinoma in situ extends well beyond the main tumor  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 37                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm  The entire specimen including the axillary tail and underlying breast parenchyma measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  The nipple is 4 0cm from the superior margin and 5 0cm from the inferior margin of the skin ellipse  There is a healed horizontal incision in the medial half of the skin ellipse  which measures 3 0cm in length  The incision is 2 8cm from the superior skin margin  2 8cm from the inferior skin margin and 3 5cm from the medial margin  On sectioning through the breast parenchyma the tissue directly beneath the skin incision reveals a firm  yellow  well demarcated mass with an irregular border  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm in dimension  Centrally there is a hemorrhagic region  measuring REMOVED_DATE in diameter  In addition  there are regions of yellow chalky  slightly firm fat between the mass and the overlying skin incision  The mass appears to abut the inferior inked margin  In addition  the mass is 0 3cm from the closest deep margin The tumor mass is 5 0cm from the superior margin  Sectioning through the remainder of the breast parenchyma reveals focal regions where there is increased white  rubbery fibrosis  No other nodules or firm areas are identified grossly  Multiple lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail region  the largest of these measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and the smallest measures 0 1cm in diameter  Section Code A E   tumor and inferior and deep margins F   medial superior quadrant G   medial inferior quadrant  near tumor H   lateral inferior quadrant I   lateral superior quadrant J   nipple K   biopsy site  skin L P   axillary tail lymph nodes Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  WHITE 03 OPERATING ROOM REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 55 CLINICAL DATA  Thirty nine year old with breast carcinoma  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b  Complete response to chemotherapy  Now for mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LEFT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN DENSE FIBROUS SCAR TISSUE WITH CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HEMOSIDERIN DEPOSITION  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTIONS TO SUTURE MATERIAL AND FAT NECROSIS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Resection margins are free of tumor  Metastatic carcinoma in 3 of 8 lymph nodes  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 54     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a 27 x 20 x 6cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 26 x 15cm overlying skin ellipse which contains a 3 5cm long scar in the outer quadrant  4cm lateral to the 5cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  Cross sectioning of the scar reveals a 1 5cm in diameter ill defined  white fibrous tissue   2cm beneath the scar  with surrounding fat necrosis but no gross evidence of tumor  This scar tissue is at least 1 5cm from the closest inferior resection margin  A random section of this fibrous area is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the breast consists of mostly of mature  yellow adipose tissue  which is intersected by scant  white  fibrous strands  No areas grossly suspicious of tumor are identified  The axillary tail measures 9 x 5 x 3cm and contains several tan  soft to rubbery lymph nodes  Section Code B F   cross sections through scar and entire remaining biopsy cavity G   nipple H Q   lymph nodes Resident  Sigrid Regauer  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Checked.
