tions  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast lumpectomy  is a oriented breast re excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm skin ellipse with a 2 0cm long well healed  oblique scar  The surgeon has denoted the superior aspect with a short stitch  and the lateral aspect with a long stitch  The superior half of the specimen is inked blue and the inferior half is inked black  Specimen is then sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic area abutting the deep resection margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm rubbery  firm white area abutting close to the inferior half of the specimen  A poorly demarcated  white  rubbery  firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lies at the deep aspect of the superior resection margin  This specimen is entirely submitted proceeding medially to laterally in cassettes A through E  with the described lesions in cassettes B  C and D  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right final shaved margins  are four fragments of focally cauterized fibroadipose tissue measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Since the specimen is received in four separate pieces  the specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely with the