ived fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire in place  A short black suture designates the superior margin  and a long black suture designates the lateral margin  The inferior margin is inked black  the superior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm cavity containing bright yellow  gritty material  The cavity comes to 0 1cm of the medial and superior margins and is 0 8cm of the lateral  1 1cm of the inferior  0 5cm of the posterior  and greater than 2 0cm of the anterior margin  The remaining cut surface displays focally dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the anterior end en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the posterior end en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  additional deep lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow to pink lobulated fibrofatty tissue with a non designated black suture along one aspect  The non designated sutured aspect is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei i