 we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  Right breast   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of fatty tissue with localizing wire  Sectioning reveals fat and a small amount of rubbery  white tissue  which focally forms a poorly circumscribed nodule  0 7cm in diameter  The specimen is entirely submitted in A   E  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm unremarkable breast fragment with localizing needle in place  which is entirely submitted in F   J with area corresponding to calcification in G and H  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   1   BIOPSY  NO DISCRETE LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   2   BIOPSY  NO AREA GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Car