ed dark red hemorrhagic cavity  located 1 0cm from the lateral  1 3cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the anterior  2 4cm from the inferior  and 4 5cm from the superior margins  The cavity is filled with dark red clotted blood and the walls are slightly indurated and contain a metal clip  The surrounding area is tan yellow to white  rubbery and lobulated  There are numerous cystic nodular areas containing thick tan white pasty material diffusely located throughout this area  This abuts the anterior  posterior and superior margins  comes to 0 5cm from the inferior  0 8cm from the lateral  and 1 0cm from the medial margins  There is a minimum amount of uninvolved tissue consisting of tan yellow to pink unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Medial margin  radially sectioned   B C  Hemorrhagic cavity with anterior and posterior margins  D  Inferior margin  E  Anterior and posterior margins  F  Superior and posterior margins  G  Lateral margin  radially sectioned   P U  Additional sections of parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue left axilla  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented irregular tan yellow to pink rubbery nodule  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow homogeneous rubbery cut surface with multiple tan yellow well delineated nodules averaging 0 1cm in diameter and extending to the closest margin of the resection  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional media