rotein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm fibrofatty breast tissue  There is a short stitch designated as superior and a long stitch designated as lateral by surgeon  The specimen is inked as follows  medial blue  lateral black  superior orange  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow white nodule with a central hemorrhagic area  consistent with a previous biopsy site  This area is 0 2cm away from the closest  medial  blue  margin  Sections are submitted as follows  A  section of nodule with closest  medial  blue  margin  B F  remainder of nodule  mass   G  representative sections away from nodule  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel right axilla hot and blue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm adipose tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins medial half of cavity   are multiple fragments of unoriented fibrofatty breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate  The fragments are sectioned and submitted entirely in I K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  uni