Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  16 MAY 98 at 10 32 CLINICAL DATA  Right mastectomy with TRAM                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1 RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADJACENT TO AND EXTENDING FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   2 ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3 METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 19 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite stromal blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins appear free of carcinoma  The metastatic carcinoma consists of small clusters of cells in the subcapsular sinus of two nodes  the metastatic cells are keratin positive  BREAST   RIGHT BREAST FLAP    BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  21 MAY 98 at 17 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 23 x 16 x 6 5cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying 22 x 10 5cm skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex  and a 6 0cm linear scar located in the lateral upper quadrant  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail is also attached to the specimen  The anterior superior surface is inked blue  the anterior inferior surface is inked green  and the deep resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm cavity filled with brown red hematoma surrounded by indurated  fibrotic parenchyma  abutting the closest deep resection margin  and 2 5cm from the closest anterior superior and 2 5cm from the closest anterior inferior resection margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma appears grossly unremarkable  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Section code  A  biopsy cavity and adjacent closest deep resection margin  B F  representative sections of the indurated wall of the biopsy cavity  G I  representative sections of the breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity  J N  representative sections of the axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue fragments  One fragment is attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm grossly unremarkable tan skin ellipse  Serial sectioning of the specimen reveals no gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted in cassette O  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  FLAP   RESECTION   report_end  , Checked.
