Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 04 CLINICAL DATA  Breast re excision of invasive ductal carcinoma with close margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED IN THE BREAST PARENCHYMA  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 12 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  1  Number of lymph nodes examined  12  Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  0  Size of largest lymph node  0 45cm metastatic deposit in a 0 6cm lymph node  Extracapsular extension  Slight  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 17 42                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm attached axillary tail  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan pink skin ellipse with 2 healed scars  4 5cm and 2 0cm  which are along the outer aspect and come to 2 0cm and 5 2cm from the nipple  respectively  The nipple is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  tan pink  and grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic cavity which comes to 0 1cm from the deep margin along the mid outer aspect  The cavity is surrounded by dense gray white fibrotic tissue with focal hemorrhage and yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  Also noted within the fibrous tissue are focal areas of induration  with no residual tumor grossly identified  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm second cavity  2 5cm superio medial to the first cavity  It comes to 0 4cm from the deep and superficial margins and is surrounded by dense gray white fibrosis and fat necrosis  Residual tumor is not identified  The remaining cut surface is 40  dense gray white fibrous tissue and 60  tan yellow lobular fibroadipose tissue with no other gross abnormalities  Evaluation of the axillary contents reveals multiple tan pink lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A C  First cavity with deep margin  D  Indurated focus surrounding first cavity with margin  E  Second cavity with deep margin  F G  Second cavity with superficial margin  H J  Lymph nodes  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Sarah P Thayer  M D  Mark Philip Eisenberg  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL OUTSIDE SLIDES RECEIVED Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 43                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  grade 2  extending to the margin of the specimen along a broad front  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  confined to the mass  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 49                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  THE CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  John P  Grabbe  M D  PATHOLOGY DEPT   CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL  REMOVED_CASE_ID  CAMBRIDGE STREET CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  97  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  22 JAN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  2 Blocks  1 , Unchecked.
