Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 30 year old woman with a history of right breast cancer diagnosed by core biopsy at an outside hospital  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH DENSE STROMAL SCLEROSIS  B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF ELEVEN LYMPH NODES  2 11   SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  11 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2 Extracapsular extension  Marked Other forms of axillary involvement  Soft tissue metastasis  Note  Sections of the lymph nodes reveal metastatic carcinoma growing in broad sheets and trabeculae with geographic zones of necrosis  The tumor nearly replaces the largest lymph node and is also noted in the adjacent soft tissue  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with focal areas of squamous differentiation  The tumor cells have abundant dense cytoplasm and enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with irregular contours  coarse vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  Numerous mitotic figures  including atypical mitoses  are readily identified with a mitotic figure count of 22 mitotic figures in 10 high powered fields  The morphologic findings are compatible with the patient s reported history of metastatic poorly differentiated carcinoma of the breast  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification are pending on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   are 2 fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue that measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  Each fragment is inked black  The largest fragment is serially sectioned to reveal a white firm cut surface with no distinct mass or lesion grossly appreciated  The first fragment is serially sectioned from one end to the other to reveal firm white tissue with no masses or lesions grossly appreciated  The entire specimens are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire large fragment sequentially submitted from one end to the other   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire smaller fragment  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary nodes   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue that aggregate to 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  Multiple candidate lymph nodes are identified ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of fibroadipose tissue with possible candidate lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 55 35PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Fi