ses  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  ENDOMETRIUM  CURETTAGE    FRAGMENT OF INACTIVE ENDOMETRIUM  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with a localization needle in place and short stitch marking the superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral margin  The specimen is orientated along the superior inferior axis and inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  lateral yellow  and medial green  On sectioning there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm ill defined mass located  0 3cm from the black inked posterior margin  0 5cm from the yellow inked lateral and green inked medial margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  and 0 8cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are taken as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior tip  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   inferior tip  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections of the mass  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative section away from mass Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with multiple possible lymph nodes dissected out  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes with one possible lymph node bisected in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  EMC   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed o