Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 02 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer   diagnosis made on the outside                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  2 NODULES  6 CM AND 1 CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 16 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY FAT  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY T Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  left breast tissue with axillary nodes  stitch on superior aspect   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail  and an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm unremarkable skin ellipse containing an unremarkable nipple and areolar complex  A stitch denotes superior  Specimen is inked and cross sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm hard  well demarcated tan pink and focally gray mass  beneath the skin ellipse  and coming to within 0 1cm of the closest margin  deep   The mass comes to within 0 4cm of the anterior skin margin  1 0cm lateral to the main mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm similar appearing hard tan nodule coming to within 0 3cm of the nearest margin  anterior  red   The tissue surrounding this nodule is firm  rubbery  and white mixed with yellow  Section code  A  Tumor with closest margin  B   B  Tumor with anterior margin  C   C D  Sections of tumor  E  Satellite nodule with closest margin  anterior F  Tissue surrounding tumor  G  Away from tumor  The axillary tail is bisected for lymph nodes  and submitted in R W  Designated  right breast tissue  stitch superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm skin ellipse with a nipple areolar complex  with tan soft material within the nipple  Specimen is inked and cross sectioned to reveal diffuse firm rubbery white and tan tissue  several areas of palpable firmness  One of these measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and comes to within 0 2cm of the nearest margin  anterior   There is a second area of ill defined firm grittiness  beneath the skin ellipse  and coming to within 1 0cm of the nearest margin  anterior   These later sections are in H through J respectively  Further sections are submitted from medial to lateral in K through Q  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Checked.
