 In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with attached REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm unremarkable skin ellipse and stitches designating the margins with one stitch respresenting the superior margin  two stitches the medial margin  The specimen is inked in black overlaid with blue superiorly  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate white tan firm tumor mass  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  the firm nodule approaches the superior resection margin and is 0 4cm from the inferior resection margin  0 4cm from the deep margin and 0 6cm from the medial margin and 1 5cm from the lateral margin  Frozen section is resubmitted in cassette A  Two closest resection margins  Superior  submitted in B and C  Tumor with deep margins submitted in D  A representative section of the main breast tissue submitted in E and F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue from which multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm are dissected away and submitted entirely in cassettes G through K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  New superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue inked and sectioned to 